{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791004645,"nonce":"iPTlkBuMD/WLy2XJElGYvbNAFbE=","title":"Every throw unwinds the whole native stack through libunwind","message":"`compiled_stack_functions` (crates/ash_interp/src/interpreter/stack.rs) runs `_Unwind_Backtrace` over the full native stack on every captured exception stack, looking for compiled frames to interleave with the interpreter's, then classifies each frame through `native_image_owns_pc`. On macOS arm64 the profile of a throw-heavy loop is almost all libunwind (`CFI_Parser::parseFDEInstructions`, `UnwindCursor::step`, FDE/CIE parsing) plus dyld image lookups.\n\n**Reproducer:** crates/ash/test/tests/TestRetierSnapshot.hx (3M throws, each caught by `step`) with `ASH_RETIER_TEST_PLAIN=0`. A copy at 200k iterations, Mac:\n\n| mode | 200k throws |\n|---|---|\n| interp (before) | ~8 s (~40 us/throw) |\n| interp (after the no-compiled-code skip) | 0.19 s |\n| hybrid / jit | 1.44 s (~7 us/throw), still libunwind-bound |\n| AOT | 0.46 s |\n\nThe full 3M-throw interp run took 119.5 s at HEAD and 123 s at 5aa28fd, against the 120 s timeout in crates/ash_cli/tests/osr_retier.rs, so `forced_snapshots_from_ordinary_and_osr_entries_preserve_live_state` timed out in its interp step whenever the Mac was loaded. Not a regression from today: same at 5aa28fd.\n\nPart 1 (interp): with no compiled code registered the walk can only return empty, so it is now skipped (`jit_map::any`). 3M-throw interp run: 119.5 s -\u003e 5.4 s.\n\nPart 2 (open): compiled modes still pay the unwind per throw. On Apple arm64 every frame keeps a frame record (the existing continuation after the unwinder relies on that), so a frame-pointer walk from the current frame could replace `_Unwind_Backtrace` there. Needs the trace-coverage tests (parity_matrix, unit CallStack cases, the exception-trace work in 2fc5051/3eb6b20/2b0a4cc) to hold.","files":null}]}